-| `attach_codesys` | **NEW** - take over a CODESYS the user opened by hand, e.g. to work in the project they have open. Writes the attach script (`%LOCALAPPDATA%\Codesys-MCP-Master\attach-codesys-mcp.py`), which installs the MCP watcher and returns; CODESYS stays usable. By default (`auto`, default true) the MCP runs it itself: it presses Tools > Scripting > Execute Script File... of that CODESYS through the Windows accessibility interface of its menu, chosen by PID (never the foreground window), puts the script path into the Open dialog with window messages and confirms it, without moving the mouse or typing; success is checked by the `[MCP]` title marker, then the session is taken over (about 3 s on SP18). With several CODESYS opened by hand it does not guess: it lists them and the agent asks the user, then calls again with `pid`. When the automation cannot run (a modal dialog open in that CODESYS, a menu that differs, not Windows) the reply names the step and why, and the user runs the script by hand: Tools > Scripting > Execute Script File... (`auto: false` skips the automation; `waitSeconds` is how long it then waits). The MCP never closes or kills an attached CODESYS: `shutdown_codesys` (and the server stopping with `--no-keep-alive`) only detach, and `killExisting` spares it; with the default keep-alive the attach watcher stays and the next session takes it over. `waitSeconds: 0` only writes the script and reports its path, no automation. A shortcut that starts CODESYS with `--runscript="%LOCALAPPDATA%\Codesys-MCP-Master\attach-codesys-mcp.py"` skips the menu step (the server rewrites the script on every start). An MCP-driven CODESYS shows `[MCP]` at the end of its window title |
+| `attach_codesys` | **NEW** - take over a CODESYS the user opened by hand, e.g. to work in the project they have open. Writes the attach script (`%TEMP%\Codesys-MCP-Master\attach-codesys-mcp.py`), which installs the MCP watcher and returns; CODESYS stays usable. By default (`auto`, default true) the MCP runs it itself: it presses Tools > Scripting > Execute Script File... of that CODESYS through the Windows accessibility interface of its menu, chosen by PID (never the foreground window), puts the script path into the Open dialog with window messages and confirms it, without moving the mouse or typing; success is checked by the `[MCP]` title marker, then the session is taken over (about 3 s on SP18). With several CODESYS opened by hand it does not guess: it lists them and the agent asks the user, then calls again with `pid`. When the automation cannot run (a modal dialog open in that CODESYS, a menu that differs, not Windows) the reply names the step and why, and the user runs the script by hand: Tools > Scripting > Execute Script File... (`auto: false` skips the automation; `waitSeconds` is how long it then waits). The MCP never closes or kills an attached CODESYS: `shutdown_codesys` (and the server stopping with `--no-keep-alive`) only detach, and `killExisting` spares it; with the default keep-alive the attach watcher stays and the next session takes it over. `waitSeconds: 0` only writes the script and reports its path, no automation. A shortcut that starts CODESYS with `--runscript="%TEMP%\Codesys-MCP-Master\attach-codesys-mcp.py"` skips the menu step (the server rewrites the script on every start). An MCP-driven CODESYS shows `[MCP]` at the end of its window title |
 | `launch_codesys_with_project` | **NEW** - Launch a (potentially different) CODESYS install and open a project in it, detached from this MCP (no IPC, no watcher). For cross-version inspection or handing the user an IDE on another install. Asks first when other CODESYS of that install run (`otherInstances`, as for `launch_codesys`) |
 | `shutdown_codesys` | Shut down the persistent CODESYS instance. Unsaved projects are never thrown away unasked: the call refuses and lists them; the agent asks the user and calls again with `unsavedChanges`: `save`, `discard` or `keep-open` (the server stopping with `--no-keep-alive` keeps it open). An attached one (`attach_codesys`) is only detached and stays open. Without a CODESYS of its own it kills orphans: CODESYS an ended MCP session started, never one opened by hand or used by another live session |
 | `get_codesys_status` | Get current state, PID, execution mode |
